From 6197fb6fb2417679c2dbe52926586905d8a3cef8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:22:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 175/177] urltest: fallbacks without outbounds, block as a
 fallback, a bound on tests at once

A URL test may have fallbacks and no outbounds: what is left of a rule whose
provider took every server away. A block fallback answers by refusing: it is
chosen when nothing before it answers, never tested, and its refusals are no
failures of a member. No more than four URL tests run at once in the process:
groups run their rounds at their own times, ten members at once, and bursts of
TLS hellos are what operators' DPI freezes.
